@startuml

title Subscription and live updates

participant Client1
participant Server
participant Client2

group subscribe after joining
alt socket subscription
Client1->Server: SubscribeGameRequest over TCP
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(current snapshot)
note over Client1, Server
Future updates use the same TCP object stream.
end note
else RMI subscription
Client1->Client1: export RemoteGameUpdateListener
Client1->Server: subscribe(request, listener stub)
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(current snapshot)
note over Client1, Server
Future updates use a reverse RMI connection to
the hostname and callback port advertised by Client1.
end note
end
end

Client2->Server: game command
Server->Server: update model and build snapshot

alt live update reaches Client1
Server-->Client1: GameViewUpdate(snapshot)
Client1->Client1: listener refreshes CLI or GUI
else RMI callback is unreachable
Server -x Client1: onUpdate fails
Server->Server: remove failed subscriber
Client1->Server: SnapshotRequest (manual refresh)
Server-->Client1: GameOperationResult(current snapshot)
end

Server-->Client2: GameOperationResult(same snapshot)

note over Client1, Client2
The command response and the subscriber update are separate messages.
A successful command response does not prove that an RMI callback is reachable.
end note

@enduml
